        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-29T09:31:13+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T09:31:13+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T23:01:13Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T23:01:13Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of WA extends a ridge over southern parts of the state while a weak trough lies across central Australia near the norther border. The high will drift over the southeast today and into the Tasman Sea on Friday, allowing a trough and low pressure system to move across SA on Friday. A brief high pressure system settles over SA on Saturday before another trough and low starts to move across from WA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
